{
  "case_id": "2005-04-848",
  "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No. 04-848"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Federal Tort Claims Act's postal-matter exception bars any claim arising out of the failure of the Postal Service to fulfill its duty to deliver mail to its intended destination on time and in good condition, but does not bar any claim arising out of ordinary negligence that happens to occur while the tortfeasor is delivering mail."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States Postal Service",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government argues for a much broader construction that would bar all claims that arise from the handling of mail."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Mr. Radmore, what was the purpose of the enactment of the waiver of Federal sovereign immunity here? Was it to allow recovery for auto accidents occurring by postal trucks?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, I guess we've already construed it broadly, haven't we, in -- or, excuse me -- yes, construed the waiver broadly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But you're using --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the broad interpretation that the Government asks for, and that the Third Circuit followed, was that \"negligent transmission\" covered anything that occurred to the mail from the time the mail was dropped off at the Post Office until it arrived at a"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It falls within the word \"transmission,\" but the relevant phrase is \"negligent transmission of mail or postal matter.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, how is mail- --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First of all, the decision to put it into a mailbox is a uniquely postal --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. MILLETT",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are -- there are 700 -- about 700 slip-and-fall cases a year, but the vast, vast majority of those are slipping in a building on, you know, a slippery floor, which we concede liability for. Probably, you know -- less than a dozen, around ten or so a year, thus far."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. MILLETT",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If we break -- if we break -- whatever damage is done to the mail, and the package in the mail, the liquid in the mail cannot be sued over. That is -- and I think Petitioners agree -- damage to and from the mail --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Except that you -- my biggest hangup -- and I wish you'd go through your distinguishing of it again -- is the -- is the Kosak case. Carrying the mail in a mail truck is the handling of the mail. There is no doubt that it's the handling of the mail."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if the postman throws the box onto the porch and hits somebody there, you say that's within the exception?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. MILLETT",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "practical reason that you don't have the sheer volume of claims, against which the Postal Service is largely defenseless, that you have when you start talking --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "distinction. You say there is no liability for the package that falls off the back of the truck, but there is liability if the truck hits another vehicle. I really don't understand the basis for that distinction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. RADMORE",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The choice of what to take into the mail would be covered by the discretionary-function exception of the exceptions to the Federal Tort Claims Act. So, I think that's a red herring."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0002-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about the practical problem that was raised that, in the automobile accident, there's witnesses, there's a police report, usually; but a slip-and-fall over mail, nobody's around, these are easily made up, and the Post Office has no opportunity to check?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States Postal Service",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RADMORE: But that's -- that's the situation in any tort. There doesn't have to be a police report, necessarily, in an automobile accident. And in a -- any slip-and-fall or any tort, beyond the motor vehicle accident, it's the same situation. It's not unique to the Post Office."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RADMORE: That's what you'd have to do to a UPS or a Federal Express employee. And I believe Solicitor General's response to Justice Ginsburg question about the number of claims that you have a year -- I believe the Solicitor General said situations like this arise ten times a year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Office's own handbook dealing with the handling of negligence cases sets forth procedures and policies that deal exactly with this type of circumstance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If we were to look at the handbook -- I think, Justice Kennedy referred to the handbook, and that section 141 of the Postal Investigation Handbook talks about claims that arise for personal injury or property damage during the delivery of the mail."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, according to the Government, there's only been ten a year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-848",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8c327f505ffff62c64b665d8cf9f2ccec8fdfdb6d02a9c91575d4193d338b561",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8c327f505fff-0003-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "[Whereupon, at 11:01 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.]"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
